DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis\, Vrykounta (Olympos)
LOCATION:Olympos / Vrykounta\, Karpathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 28-29 August the people of Olympos walk down to the underground church of Agios Ioannis at Vrykounta\, an ancient site on the far north coast: park at Avlona and walk about 90 minutes down the old path\, carrying a sleeping bag because everyone spends the night on the stone terraces around the church. Braised goat\, chickpea soup and loukoumades are served at long tables\, and the mantinades and dancing to lyra go on until dawn. Pack water and a torch\; there is only a small canteen.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#olympos-vrykounta-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-vrykounta-olympo
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#olympos-vrykounta-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-vrykounta-olympo
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:karpathos-mesochori-panigiri-of-panagia-mesochoritissa-mesochori-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Mesochoritissa\, Mesochori
LOCATION:Mesochori\, Karpathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Mesochori\, a car-free village of stepped lanes on the west coast\, celebrates the Nativity of the Virgin at Panagia Mesochoritissa\, the church built over the village spring\, with vespers on the 7th and a feast with lyra and laouto on the square. Volada also feasts on 8 September. Park at the top of the village and walk down.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#mesochori-panigiri-of-panagia-mesochoritissa-mesochori
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#mesochori-panigiri-of-panagia-mesochoritissa-mesochori
END:VEVENT
